WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.370
You hit send.

2
00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:04.110
A message leaves a laptop in a bedroom.

3
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.070
Zoom out.

4
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.970
The house.

5
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.010
The street.

6
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.630
The whole country.

7
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.550
Then the globe, glittering
with billions of devices.

8
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.690
Only one should get your message.

9
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.010
But first, it reaches a box
by the front door, and stops.

10
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.750
So how does it find that one computer?

11
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.070
Is it sent to every device,
so the right one keeps it?

12
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.250
In this mission, you'll see how an IP
address identifies a device on a network.

13
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.370
You'll find that every packet
carries a destination IP address.

14
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.690
And you'll meet routers, which
connect networks together.

15
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.880
Your mission: explain how your data
finds one computer among billions online.
